# Flutter & Dart Coding Guidelines

This project's rules live in its `CLAUDE.md` files, not here. Read them before writing or
modifying any code: the root file always applies, plus the file for the layer you are editing.
If the `@` references below do not resolve, open the same paths and read them anyway.

- @CLAUDE.md — project overview, layer map, standards common to every layer
- @lib/data/CLAUDE.md — API, storage, SDK integration (Service / DTO)
- @lib/domain/CLAUDE.md — entities and pure domain logic, no framework deps
- @lib/presentation/CLAUDE.md — screens, viewmodels (Cubit), widgets (MVVM + Bloc)
- @lib/presentation/design_system/CLAUDE.md — design tokens, context-free components
- @lib/presentation/router/CLAUDE.md — route declarations, object passing, transitions
- @lib/utils/CLAUDE.md — domain-agnostic general utilities

A `CLAUDE.md` always wins over this file. To change a rule, edit that `CLAUDE.md` only —
never copy it back here.

